      <pattern name="identity-value condition emission" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipResolverService.cs">BuildFetchXml's per-descriptor per-identity-value condition emission — org ids bind exactly as Organization descriptor values do on the systemuser path.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Read the post-041 resolver, post-042 evaluator, investigation 02 §2.4/§3.</step>
    <step order="1">Extend ResolveByContactAsync: behind a new explicit option, populate the identity's OrganizationIds from the contact's active junction rows before FetchXml construction; org-typed descriptors (registry-filtered) then emit conditions naturally; keep byRole attribution so the evaluator can distinguish org-derived from contact-derived ids (provenance for FR-30 and for level assignment).</step>
    <step order="2">Wire the evaluator's org-expansion term: for each org-derived record id, contribute at the owning org's baseline (042 reader), gated on the org's standing flag; route through the Secure suppression hook.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire AccessConferringOnly=true into ComposeForSystemUserAsync's membership fallback branch (flag-off path of 036); confirm the flag-on branch is untouched.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests per the closed set (resolver-shape + evaluator-term + suppression + fallback).</step>
    <step order="5">Build + tests; publish-size measurement per §10.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>ENCODE, DO NOT DECIDE: if implementation reaches a point where a NON-standing derived contribution (contact-derived term 3, or org-derived with no org standing grant) needs a level to be useful (register B-1 says derived access is "default-on" but no FR assigns its level), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the options (ViewOnly floor / standing-gated as implemented) — do not invent a default level.</trigger>
    <trigger>If binding org ids on the contact path breaks the M10 endpoint-contract byte-compatibility for existing membership API consumers, STOP and surface it (investigation 02 §8 M10 note) rather than shipping a changed wire shape.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipResolverService.cs</output>
